WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We´re here
with Chef Danny Bowien,

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.803
founder of Mission Chinese Food.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, man.
-He´s also featured

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.607
in the sixth season of the
series "The Mind of a Chef."

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:10.410
The first three episodes are
available on Facebook Watch.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.212
-I´m so stoked to be here.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.713
-And what are we making tonight?

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.782
-Okay, so, you know, I cooked
in restaurants for a long time.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
I actually grew up
in Oklahoma City,

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:20.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I didn´t know I wanted
to be a chef.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.755
I wanted to be a optometrist for
a long time.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:22.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.991
-But anyway, I went through this
career path

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.159
of cooking in restaurants,

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:27.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
thought I wanted to be
a fine-dining chef.

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:29.896
And then I had this dish
at this Sichuan restaurant.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you had Sichuan food
before?

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Has anyone here had Sichuan?

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.267 size:84% position:42%
Do you like spicy food?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:37.070
So I was 26. I thought
I wanted to quit cooking,

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.805
and I was, like, I was over it.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had Sichuan food
for the first time.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.641
-Where did you have that?

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:42.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In San Francisco...
-Okay, great.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-at this great restaurant
called Spices II.

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:45.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, great.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, anyway,
I´m going to make a dish

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:48.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
called Chung Ching
chicken wings.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it´s, like, a very spicy,
numbing,

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.119
tingly chicken wing dish,
and it´s usually hammered

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
under a big blanket
of chili peppers.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:55.989
-Very excited about this.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´m gonna fry
some chicken wings.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, chefs like to be
know-it-alls.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.562
One day there was a debate of
who has the best chicken wings,

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
how do you make
the perfect chicken wing.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one of the guys in our
kitchen chimed in

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.234
and was like, "Well, my mom used
to work

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the Anchor Bar in Buffalo."
Buffalo, New York,

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:12.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
where the buffalo chicken wing
was created.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.041 size:78% position:39%
So we´re like, "Okay.
How did they do it?"

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.643
And they fry their wing twice.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:17.977
So that´s what we´ve done here.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we have a wing that´s been
fried and then frozen,

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then now we´re frying it
again.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.149
It´s kind of French fries.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.284 size:81% position:41%
That´s why McDonald´s
has great French fries

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
is they´re fried, frozen,
and re-fried.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you´re McDonald´s food.
-Basically.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I did grow up in Oklahoma.

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, yeah.
-So where did you grow up?

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where did you grow up?
-I grew up in New Hampshire.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:37.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, so the way we make
our chicken wings

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
is we don´t fry them at all.
-Really?

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:40.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you do?
It´s like rotisserie-style?

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, my mom actually --
the way -- we don´t even --

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.238 size:78% position:39%
My mom would just get
frozen chicken wings,

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.140
put them on a pan,
and just throw them in the oven.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.441 size:88% position:44%
-Okay, well, that works.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.677
-Nutritionally it doesn´t work.

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.145
-Yeah, well, you know, you know.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.847
-Should we have a cocktail, too,
while we´re here?

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:57.784
-Sure. So this is probably best
to drink after we eat the wings.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:58.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Great.
-But let´s put it together.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, great.
You´re in charge.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´m gonna let you do
everything.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:04.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, we should shake this up
first.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.892
This is called a Phil Collins,

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.594
that´s one of our signature
drinks at the restaurant,

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:10.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
it´s basically
coconut milk infused with gin,

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:15.969 size:88% position:44%
lemon grass, and ginger.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:16.970
And we let it set overnight.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
You want to scoop some ice
in there?

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:19.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, sure.

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:20.640 size:84% position:42%
-In these little bowls.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why do you call it
a Phil Collins?

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I mean,
I like Phil Collins a lot.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
And our beverage director
when opening,

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like --
his name´s Sam Anderson,

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.616
I was like, "Let´s make a drink
that´s, like,

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:31.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
just name it after
Phil Collins."

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.452 size:84% position:42%
And he was like, "Okay.
Let´s make something

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:34.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
that´s like a Tom Kha soup.
Like a Thai soup."

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:37.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you can pour this
into those little cups there.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You should call it
a Phil Collins

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you get drunk enough
that you see someone

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you think crossed you
in high school.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:46.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s a very specific joke
for nobody.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.268 size:75% position:38%
-I was like, "Uh..."

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:49.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
All right, so we´ll pour that
in there.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
While that´s happening,
I will take the wings out.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:55.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will help you.
Well, you hold, I´ll pour.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:58.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, great.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:00.914
Is there any pouring music?

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Could we just get
a light pouring drum roll?

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:04.117
-Phil Collins? Is there a
Phil Collins-pouring music?

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.552 size:84% position:42%
-It should be drumming.

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Drum roll ]

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
There we go!
-All right, cool.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:12.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we garnish this
with some kaffir lime leaves

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little bit of dried chili.
-Okay, great.

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is a little bit
of chili oil.

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:18.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
Wonderful.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I´m going to wait
to drink mine until after.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; Okay, well, so am I.
-´Cause, you know, you know.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:27.807
So the good things about cooking
the wings twice

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.576
is they get super, super crispy.

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:30.743
So, like, you can look at these,

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.579
they´re really super crispy.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:34.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we´re gonna drop them
in here.

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:35.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then these are
all the spices.

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:37.984 size:84% position:42%
You know, Sichuan food,
it really prides itself

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:42.121
on having things that are sweet,
salty, spicy, tingly.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.856
And that comes from this --
it´s Sichuan peppercorns.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
So Sichuan peppercorn,
fennel seed,

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:47.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
cumin seed.

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:49.596 size:75% position:38%
I forgot to grind up
the black cardamom,

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:51.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we´ll just throw those
in there whole.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:52.498 size:88% position:44%
-Okay, great. [ Laughs ]

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.167 size:81% position:41%
-Cayenne chili pepper.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I have all the stuff
premixed together

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:57.503
for the magic of television.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:58.771
Here, I´ll let you do this.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:01.908
You can just shake,
and I´ll just dump this in here.

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:06.012
-This is for those who are
watching on TV and can´t smell,

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.547
it´s kind of overwhelming.

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:08.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s intense.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you can just dump that
on this plate here.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:12.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
There we go.
-Okay, great.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.153
And then the beauty of this dish
is --

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can dump all this
on there, too.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:16.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-The beauty of this dish

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:20.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that it literally is
under a blanket.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you gonna let me eat
the premade ones?

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:23.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you can eat either.
Either, or.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can I try one now?
-Yeah, sure.

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:26.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How spicy is it?
-Try one of these.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:27.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
These are the best.
It´s pretty hot.

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:29.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s very tingly.
-Okay.

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:30.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I think that´s
from the Sichuan peppers.

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-You ready?

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can only eat one of these,
by the way,

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:35.008
at the restaurant, so let´s see
how long it takes us

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:36.109 size:88% position:44%
to take a drink of that.

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:40.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Coughs ]
All right.

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.048 size:78% position:39%
What are you feeling?
-What´s happening?

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What are you feeling now?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.752 size:75% position:38%
-It´s happening now.

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, my God!

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whew!

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:50.490
-Anybody want one of these?

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.325
No, yes, yes, pass them back.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:53.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
Pass them back.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:54.894
All right. I need a drink.

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:55.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Anyways. Cheers.

00:04:58.498 --> 00:05:00.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Cheers, that was fantastic.
Thank you so much.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.267 size:88% position:44%
Danny Bowien, everybody!

